    "summary": "Sixteen-year-old Pakistani-American high schooler Kamala Khan lives in Jersey City, daydreaming and drawing superhero fan-art celebrating Captain Marvel. Donning an antique brass bangle mailed by her grandmother in Karachi for AvengersCon, Kamala unlocks latent genetic abilities to manifest glowing \"hard-light\" crystalline shields and platforms. Navigating high school life, Muslim family traditions, and ruthless Department of Damage Control agents, Kamala unravels ancestral ties to the Noor dimension, traveling to Pakistan to understand her family's generational partition trauma.",
    "spoilerSummary": "Kamala travels back in time during the 1947 Partition of India, creating the trail of stars that saved her infant grandmother Sana. Najma seals the Noor veil, transferring energy into son Kamran. Defending her high school with friends, Kamala embraces her community name: Ms. Marvel. Tech genius Bruno reveals Kamala's genes possess a unique \"mutation\" (accompanied by the 1990s X-Men animated theme lick).",
